# Threat hunt report: attack

**Hypothesis:** An external IP brute-forced SSH on DEMO-SSH and then logged in successfully between 2026-10-25T00:00:00Z and 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z.

| | |
|---|---|
| **Verdict** | Confirmed |
| Confidence | high |
| C2's draft verdict | SUPPORTED (high confidence). C3 review: agrees |
| Analyst review required | yes: a Confirmed verdict is never acted on automatically; C2's free text names entities that appear in no evidence |
| Time window (UTC) | 2026-10-25T00:00:00Z to 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z |
| Planner | llm |
| Verification | mcp, 4/4 claims verified, replay 26/26 identical |

## 1. Summary

The hunt confirmed the hypothesis with high confidence: 4 verified finding(s) support T1078 (Valid Accounts), T1110 (Brute Force). The earliest supporting event is at 2026-10-25T00:10:00.000Z. An analyst should review the findings before acting.

**Why this verdict**

- Every part of the hypothesis has a technique with at least the minimum number of independent verified indicators.
- 1 statement(s) written by C2 name entities that appear in no evidence: C2 run note 1 mentions AG-02, which appear in no evidence.
- C2 reported SUPPORTED (high); C3's re-verification agrees.

## 2. Hunt plan

Techniques tested (required first): `T1110` Brute Force, `T1078` Valid Accounts

Success criteria:

- T1110 (Brute Force): at least 1 independent self-checked indicator(s)
- T1078 (Valid Accounts): at least 1 independent self-checked indicator(s)

Refutation criteria:

- T1110: all required sources and fields covered for the full window AND zero indicators
- T1078: all required sources and fields covered for the full window AND zero indicators

Entities named in the hypothesis: DEMO-SSH

